# descriptions
# dev-check: Diagnose dev wiki structural integrity and state consistency, then offer to auto-fix issues.
# dev-debrief: Tiered session capture with phase debriefs, decision logging, and memory harvesting.
# dev-init: Bootstrap a .dev-wiki/ directory for a project.
# dev-plan: Plan one phase at a time, informed by accumulated wiki knowledge.
# dev-scan: Deep codebase analysis producing structural knowledge for the dev-wiki.
# dev-wiki: Route dev wiki operations and enforce development lifecycle discipline.
# knowledge-wiki: Route wiki operations and enforce wiki workflow discipline.
# py-init: Scaffold or retrofit the Nana Dev Kit harness into the current directory.
# py-lint: Run linting, formatting, and type checking (ruff + mypy).
# py-review: Review the current diff against the 8-point AI PR checklist.
# py-test: Run the full test suite with coverage and report failures concisely.
# spec: Write a structured spec/contract before execution to prevent ambiguous contracts.
# wiki-absorb: Process raw entries in inbox/ into polished, cross-linked, tagged articles.
# wiki-add: Add content to inbox/ as raw entries for later processing by /wiki-absorb.
# wiki-bootstrap: Seed the wiki with foundational domain knowledge via research and batch-generation.
# wiki-consolidate: Process unconsolidated episodic entries through dedup and fact extraction.
# wiki-health: Combined wiki health tool: dashboard metrics, structural audit, and staleness marking.
# wiki-index: Build a hybrid search index over wiki articles and episodic entries.
# wiki-init: Initialize a project-specific wiki through interactive interview and scaffold.
# wiki-query: Answer questions by navigating the project wiki's knowledge base.
# wiki-registry: Manage the wiki registry (~/.claude/wikis.json).
# wiki-reorg: Restructure wiki hierarchy, create hub articles, add cross-links, normalize tags.
